==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{uder|en|LL.|prisma}}, from {{der|en|grc|πρίσματος}}, from {{der|en|grc|πρίσμα||something sawed}}, from {{m|grc|πρίζειν||to saw}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-prism.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɪzəm/|[ˈpʰɹ̠̊ɪzm̩]}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪzəm|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geometry}} A [[polyhedron]] with [[parallel]] ends of the same size and shape, the other faces being [[parallelogram]]-shaped sides.
# A transparent block in the shape of a prism (typically with triangular ends), used to split or reflect light.
# A crystal in which the faces are parallel to the [[vertical]] [[axis]].

